From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: add atomic testrawtxbatch and submitrawtxbatch package
 RPCs

Add all-or-nothing batch transaction validation and submission RPCs
(testrawtxbatch and submitrawtxbatch).

Original-Commit: ce5e6b2465d878d80caf1f1f068bba9a84908f60
Original-Patch: ecash/015
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Complete atomic batch admission at its first RPC owner using the existing ABC standard and next-block consensus script checks, staged dependency resolution, exact pre-insertion capacity reservation, one snapshot publication and ordered batched notifications. Preserve parallel raw decoding and reject malformed inputs deterministically. Move fee-controller diagnostics, concrete batched relay and parallel resolved-input script processing to their actual later feature owners; remove the historical serial-decoder regression/restoration churn. Capacity failure accepts nothing and evicts no existing transactions; ordinary admission and consensus remain unchanged. Retain all original assertions; add memory-boundary, no-partial-admission, parallel-error and two-node 40-transaction relay/mining regressions. Manual109Bitcoin/123Avalanche and dedicated functional checks pass; clean progression gates remain required.

